    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0822" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1791: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-05T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                                1920—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1615. If London has not repeated its No. 1560, October 30, noon,<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d748-f1"/> to you request that it do so.</p>
                <p>Do all you can to cooperate with British in Paris in support of British
                    representations that French pay debts due Chinese Eastern <pb facs="0823"
                        n="725" xml:id="pg725"/> for maintenance and transportation of Czech troops
                    over Chinese Eastern Railway in order to assist railway in its present financial
                    difficulties and insure uninterrupted operation of the line.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
